          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most painted houses, DAP Dynaflex 230 is the right default: easy to apply, paintable, and flexible enough for real exterior joints. Move to Sashco Big Stretch where joints keep cracking, OSI Quad for vinyl and fiber cement, Geocel 2300 for metal and masonry, and GE Advanced Silicone 2 for glass and unpainted metal.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The product is only half the job. Cut out the old bead, clean to bare surfaces, size the joint with backer rod, push the bead and tool it, then paint it once the label allows. Do that and even a mid-priced sealant will outlast a premium tube laid over old caulk.
